WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.634
-Our next guest will be

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.634
performing her solo show,

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:05.434
"Imagine I'm Someone Else,"

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:08.200
at Union Hall
in New York City November 2nd.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.734
Please welcome
the very funny Isabel Hagen.

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:12.868
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:15.868
[ The Roots playing
bright funk ]

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.667
♪♪

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:18.868
-Thank you.

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:20.334
Thank you so much!

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:23.601
Oh, it is so good
to be back in New York.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.334
I just did a show
in a small town in Missouri

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.100
and they had me at a hotel

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.234
and at the hotel,

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:32.968
there was a poster of me
in the elevator.

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:35.100
And I'm not famous...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.234
...so, to other people,
it just kind of looked

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:37.434
like I put it there.

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:39.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:40.801
And so, anytime
I got on the elevator,

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:44.300
I just to pray no one else
would be on

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.901
with me and my dumb poster.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:46.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:48.033
And I got on the first day

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:49.133
and there were two people,

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.934
so I quickly like stepped back

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:53.834
to kind of block it
with my body.

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:56.400
But I missed and I just
sort of stood next to it.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.501 --> 00:00:59.667
The saddest showing off.

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:01.000
"Look familiar?"
[ Nervous laugh ]

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:05.701
But I flew home from Missouri
and there was a kid behind me

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:07.634
who cried the whole flight.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.834
[ Awws ]
Yeah, not a baby, a child.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:10.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.400
He knew what he was doing.
Oh.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.434
[ Laughter ]
But about two hours in,

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:16.901
he spoke amongst the crying

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:18.934
and he was British.

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.834
And I was like, "Oh.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.567
[ Laughter ]
All is forgiven.

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:24.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:27.200
That's adorable."

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.968
[ English accent ] Mummy,
you let me watch the telly.

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:32.067
Let him watch the telly.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:33.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.033
He's clearly a genius...

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:36.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:39.100
...and very charming.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.067
That's why I couldn't have like
a British boyfriend, you know.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.367
I'd let him treat me like crap.

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:43.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:44.801
[ English accent ]
I've cheated on you.

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:45.968
"Say it again."

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:49.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:52.234
So, I'm a comedian and I also
am a classical musician.

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:53.901
I play the viola.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:56.267
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yeah, alright, yeah.

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.400
I live a bit of a double life

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.801
and I still play viola gigs
around New York City.

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:05.300
And I have a boyfriend now,
but in the past,

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.834
I have gone home with a guy
after a viola gig.

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:11.934
Yeah, I do very well, alright?

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:13.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:15.834
No. The worst part about it is
just the next morning,

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:17.267
doing the walk of shame

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:18.634
with the viola, you know?

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:22.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:23.834
[ Applause ]

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.000
I get in my head.
I'm like,

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.133
"Oh, if I had a guitar,
that'd be cooler."

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:29.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:31.634
People would see me,
they're like, "Oh, she's cool.

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:32.968
This chick's in a band.

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:35.801
Of course she got some action."

00:02:35.801 --> 00:02:38.133
[ Laughter ]
With the viola, it's just like,

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:39.267
Oh, little Miss Goody-Goody

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:40.834
got laid
after the symphony concert.

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:43.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:47.901
What a nerdy whore."

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:51.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:53.300
So, I do comedy
and I play viola

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.334
and people ask me
sometimes like,

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:58.701
"Oh, do you ever combine
the two in your act?"

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:02.534
And I usually say no
because I'm not a hack.

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:03.634
But, uh --

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:05.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:08.067
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:12.000
But enough people have asked,
so I've decided to humor them.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.400
So, if you don't mind,
I'm going to play a little viola

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.901
and then do a little standup

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:17.834
and we'll see how it goes
together, alright?

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:21.934
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:23.267
Little viola, little standup.

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:25.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:28.167
[ Playing upbeat tune ]

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:32.934
♪♪

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:35.133
My boyfriend and I are thinking
of having a threesome.

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:38.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.234
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:46.334
The good news is we're both
down for the threesome.

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:47.667
That's the good news.

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:50.133
The bad news is he, of course,
imagines it like him,

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:51.868
another girl, me.

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:53.934
I imagine it me, another guy,

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:54.834
another girl.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:58.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:00.901
[ Cheering ]

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:05.934
[ Playing somber tune ]

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:15.767
♪♪

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:16.901
-Whoo!

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:19.267
-My friend asked me
how I stay so skinny

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:20.968
and I don't know what
to tell her.

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:23.501
For me, it's just genetics,
you know, like my grandma

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:24.968
also starves herself.

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:28.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:35.133
[ Playing jaunty tune ]

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:43.434
♪♪

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:45.968
♪♪

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:48.667
I deal with a lot
of negative self-talk

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:50.801
[ Laughter ]
and my therapist was like,

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:54.968
"Well, try talking to yourself
the way you would a good friend.

00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:57.267
You wouldn't say all those
mean things to her."

00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:59.167
I'm like,
"Yeah, not to her face."

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:02.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.167
[ Cheering ]

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:08.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.434 --> 00:05:11.434
[ Playing jaunty tune ]

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:21.434
♪♪

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:24.601
♪♪

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:27.400
[ Whistling, cheering,
and applause ]

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.968
My boyfriend wants
to settle down and I'm like,

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:34.767
"Look, buddy, I got a lot
of things I want to do

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.167
before I settle down, you know?

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:37.801
Like find the right person."

00:05:37.801 --> 00:05:39.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:40.901
I've been Isabel Hagen.
Thank you so much.

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:42.901
[ The Roots playing
upbeat funk ]

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:44.868
[ Whistling ]
-Come on, buddy!

00:05:44.868 --> 00:05:46.200
[Indistinct]

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.834
♪♪

00:05:47.834 --> 00:05:49.133
Isabel Hagen!

00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:51.434
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:56.634
Isabel will be at Union Hall
in New York City November 2nd.

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:57.968
We'll be right back, everybody.

